{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKbtpRKynjLysWYwhNwt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Fix:** commit `e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e` (\"TRUNK-6646: Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup\", PR #6145, by jwnasambu). The PR number comes from the commit subject; I did not check it separately.\n\n**Cause:** `normalizeEnvVariableKey` lowercases every environment variable name and turns `_` into `.` unless the name is in `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`. So `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME` became `create.database.username`, and the wizard's lookup of `create_database_username` never found it. Setup then fell back to the defaults (root, no password).\n\n**Fix:** the commit adds the credential variables (and several others) to `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`, so they keep their underscores. It also makes the driver-class, `import_test_data`, remote-URL and admin-password-locked reads accept the env-var names. Tests cover the new behaviour.\n\n**Evidence, best first:**\n\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java:197-201`: `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS` now includes `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME`, `CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `CREATE_USER_USERNAME` and `CREATE_USER_PASSWORD`, among others.\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java:1948-1953`: `normalizeEnvVariableKey` skips the dot conversion for whitelisted keys.\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java:340-343`: environment variables are normalized and copied into the script properties.\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java:368-374`: the wizard reads `create_database_username` and `create_database_password` from those properties (line range approximate, from the grep hits at lines 370 and 372).\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java:1-92`: new unit tests asserting the underscore-preserving keys and that non-whitelisted keys still convert to dots.\n- `openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterTest.java:163-242`: new end-to-end tests feeding `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME` and related variables through `initializeWizardFromResolvedPropertiesIfPresent` (range from the diff hunk).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 197, \"endLine\": 201},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 1948, \"endLine\": 1953},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 340, \"endLine\": 343},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 368, \"endLine\": 374},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java\", \"startLine\": 1, \"endLine\": 92},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterTest.java\", \"startLine\": 163, \"endLine\": 242},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"commit\": \"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"pr\": 6145},\n  {\"ticket\": \"TRUNK-6646\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":29837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1712},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transf